    "turn_text": "I thank you Scott Shannon hour two Sean Hannity show toll-free it is eight hundred nine four one Sean if you want to be a part of the program I mean the fact that we're getting little to zero information about what is happening with these balloons and and why the inaction in the beginning and the lack of communication even with elected officials is sort of breathtaking, having the head of NORAD suggesting, wow, this might have something to do with extraterrestrials. I'm like, really? We now have had US jets down four objects in eight days. This is after, by the way, we have the initial incursion into US airspace that started in Alaska went down the coast of Canada into Idaho all the way across to our missile silo sites in the great state of Montana and down you know to the Midwestern states and and the plain states and and Kansas and Missouri then Kentucky then the Carolinas where they shoot the first one down And after criticism, they finally got the message that whatever these objects are, they better take them out sooner rather than later. Here's the problem. Remember, we are not recognizing that these objects are even entering our airspace. How could we have such a gaping hole in our defense systems? and why the silence and why the lack of communication now senator steve deans of montana along with you know frankly every state senator uh... or u.s. senator you know who's been having to deal with these balloons flying over their states they're pissed off you can't blame them Steve Danes tweeted out the lack of communication from the Biden administration regarding closing Montana airspace last night and the recent shoot downs that took place over Alaska and Canada is unacceptable. He said the top priority administration should be the safety and security that people of the United States, keeping the people informed as a key part of fulfilling that duty. President Biden owes the people of Montana and the country an immediate and full explanation. Without information, the public, the media are left to rely on leaks, speculation and worst of all, disinformation from foreign governments. I'm in direct contact with the Pentagon regarding the object in Montana's airspace and we receive frequent updates and the people of Montana still have questions about the Chinese spy balloon that flew over our state last week. And he's going to continue to request answers to all of this. And then I don't know, you know, Biden is now out there saying that this is not a major breach. How can anyone make that assessment that the communist Chinese were able to fly into and all around the continental United States, after starting in Alaska. And it took us some citizen noticing, you know, what is the size of three buses. I mean, to recognize that this was even over our airspace and lawmakers rightly want accountability because none of this makes any sense at all. And then of course, my favorite is NORAD Commander doesn't rule out the possibility that extraterrestrials or aliens might be the unidentified objects. That really helps the American people out with intelligence. Anyway, Senator Steve Danes of the great state of Montana back with us. Senator, how are you?",
